---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'June 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — ContrastLab"
  description="ContrastLab privacy policy. Learn how we handle your data, local storage, cookies, and third-party services including Google AdSense."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="padding: 72px 24px 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); background: var(--color-canvas-soft);">
      <div style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-violet); margin-bottom: 12px;">Legal</p>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 12px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-mute);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Prose content -->
    <section style="padding: 56px 24px 80px; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="prose-content">

        <p>This Privacy Policy describes how ContrastLab ("we," "us," or "our") handles information when you use this website (the "Service"). We've written this policy to be straightforward about what data is involved and why.</p>

        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>

        <h3>Information you provide directly</h3>
        <p>ContrastLab does not require an account and does not collect your name, email address, or any other personal information during normal use of the tool.</p>
        <p>If you contact us by email, we receive the information you include in that message — your email address and anything else you choose to share. We use this only to respond to your inquiry.</p>

        <h3>Usage data</h3>
        <p>We may collect anonymized, aggregated data about how the tool is used — for example, which features are accessed most frequently. If analytics tools are used in the future, this section will be updated accordingly and any such tools will be configured to respect user privacy.</p>

        <h2>2. Local storage</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab stores the following data in your browser's local storage:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Saved palettes:</strong> Color pairs you choose to save using the "Save current" feature.</li>
          <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> Whether you've selected light or dark mode.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This data never leaves your device. It is not transmitted to our servers. It persists until you clear your browser's storage or manually delete palettes within the tool.</p>
        <p>To remove this data, use your browser's developer tools or clear site data from your browser settings.</p>

        <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab itself does not set cookies for tracking purposes.</p>
        <p>If third-party services (such as advertising or analytics providers) are integrated in the future, those services may set their own cookies. This policy will be updated before any such integrations are added, and where legally required, consent will be obtained.</p>

        <h2>4. Google AdSense</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab may display advertisements served by Google AdSense. If AdSense is active on a page, Google may use cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this site or other websites.</p>
        <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.</p>
        <p>Google's use of advertising cookies is governed by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

        <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab may load resources from third-party providers, such as font delivery networks. These providers may receive your IP address as part of the normal process of delivering content to your browser. We use reputable providers and do not share any additional data with them.</p>
        <p>We do not sell or share your data with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

        <h2>6. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has submitted personal information to us, please contact us and we will delete it.</p>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you are located, you may have certain rights regarding your data, including the right to access, correct, or delete personal information we hold about you.</p>
        <p>Because ContrastLab stores user data locally in your browser rather than on our servers, most user data is fully within your control. For any data held by us (such as email correspondence), contact us at <a href="mailto:support@contrastlab.com">support@contrastlab.com</a> to request access or deletion.</p>

        <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we make material changes to this Privacy Policy, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this page periodically.</p>

        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy? Email us at <a href="mailto:support@contrastlab.com">support@contrastlab.com</a>.</p>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-content {
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .prose-content p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .prose-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .prose-content h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .prose-content ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .prose-content li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .prose-content a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-link-bg-soft);
  }

  .prose-content a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .prose-content strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
